<html>

<head>
  <script type="application/jay-data">data:</script>
  <!-- REGION-OVERRIDE-NON-CONTENT (DL#200): the Card region IS linked (template=), flattened from source, but it then adds net-new layout DOM (<div class="ds-card__ribbon">) that the source template does not have. That is a structural change — a different design, not a content tweak — so `jay-stack validate` nudges you to make a *second* card template (a new variant) and link this region to it, rather than piling structure onto one flattened copy. (The same change is also unmarked drift, so DL#196 reports it too; mark it override="children" or run `jay-stack sync` to resolve the drift.) -->
  <script type="application/jay-headless" contract="../../components/card/card.jay-contract"
    template="../../components/card/card.jay-html"></script>
  <script type="application/jay-headless" contract="../../components/button/button.jay-contract"
    template="../../components/button/button.jay-html"></script>
  <title>Design System Demo — Variant</title>
  <meta name="description"
    content="A linked card region that adds structural DOM — REGION-OVERRIDE-NON-CONTENT.">
  <style>
    @scope (.cardFeatured) to (.cta) {
      .ds-card {
        border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
        border-radius: 10px;
        padding: 20px;
        background: #ffffff;
      }

      .ds-card__heading {
        font-size: 1.15rem;
        margin: 0 0 8px;
        color: #0f172a;
      }

      .ds-card__body {
        margin: 0 0 16px;
        color: #475569;
      }
    }

    @scope (.cta) {
      .ds-button {
        border: 0;
        border-radius: 6px;
        padding: 8px 14px;
        background: #2563eb;
        color: #ffffff;
        cursor: pointer;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>
  <div>
    <p>Variant: this card is linked (template=) and flattened, but it adds a structural ribbon the
      source template never had — jay-stack validate raises REGION-OVERRIDE-NON-CONTENT, pointing
      you to a second card template rather than a one-off structural override.</p>
    <jay:card ref="cardFeatured" heading="Pro" body="For growing teams that need more."
      ctaLabel="Choose Pro">
      <div class="ds-card">
        <h3 class="ds-card__heading">{heading}</h3>
        <p class="ds-card__body">{body}</p>
        <div class="ds-card__ribbon">Most popular</div>
        <jay:button ref="cta" label="{ctaLabel}"><button class="ds-button">{label}</button>
        </jay:button>
      </div>
    </jay:card>
  </div>
</body>

</html>
